                    %a{:href => "#ForInfinityPermutations"}
                      For permutation
                      = succeed "-representations" do
                        %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                          %semantics
                            %mrow
                              %mn ∞
                            %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                  %li
                    %a{:href => "#InfinityGaloisTheory"}
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mn ∞
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                      \-Galois theory
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tannaka"} Tannaka
            duality or
            %em
              Tannaka
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reconstruction+theorem"} reconstruction theorem
            are statements of the form:
          %p
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a symmetry object (e.g. a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+compact+topological+group"} locally compact topological group
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+algebra"} Hopf algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} represented
            on objects in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            %em reconstruct
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            from knowledge of the
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            –
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %msub
                    %mi Rep
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F : Rep_D(A) \to D
          %p
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Rep
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep_D(A)
            of
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representation"} representation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            on
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            that remembers these underlying objects. In a generalization, called mixed Tannakian formalism, not a single
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functors"} fiber functors
            over different bases is needed for a reconstruction. The fiber functor is necessary; for example, in the context of reconstruction of associative algebras, not remembering the underlying vector spaces results in reconstructing two different algebras with equivalent module categories (cf.
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Morita+equivalence"} Morita equivalence
          %p
            There is a general-abstract and a concrete aspect to this. The general abstract one says that an algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is reconstructible from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            on the category of
            %em all
            its modules. The concrete one says that in nice cases it is reconstructible from the category of
            %em dualizable
            (finite dimensional) modules, even if it is itself not finite dimensional.
          %p
            More precisely, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriching category
            (a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with all
            = succeed "s)." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/limit"} limit
          %ol
            %li
              %p for
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    a
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
                    in
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi V
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi A
                          %mi Mod
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
                    the
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi V
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
                    of
                    %em all
                    = succeed "-" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi A
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                    = succeed "s" do
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
                    = succeed ";" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %mi V
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                %li
                  %p
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi F
                          %mo :
                          %mi A
                          %mi Mod
                          %mo →
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : A Mod \to V
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful
                    %em
                      %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
                    ;
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                can be reconstructed as the object of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched endomorphisms
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi F
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ≃
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                          %mi Mod
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      A
                      \\simeq
                      End(F) := \int_{N \in A Mod} V(F(N), F(N))
                      \\,.
              %p
                This is just the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+Yoneda+lemma"} enriched Yoneda lemma
                in a slight disguise.
            %li
              %p
                In good cases, this
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
                is computed already by restriction to the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %msub
                        %mi Mod
                        %mi dual
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod_{dual}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dual+object"} dualizable modules
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⋯
                      %mo ≃
                      %msub
                        %mo ∫
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo ∈
                          %mi A
                          %msub
                            %mi Mod
                            %mi dual
                      %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                      %mo .
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      \\cdots \simeq \int_{N \in A Mod_{dual}} V(F(N), F(N))
                      \\,.
          %h2#statement Statement
          %p
            So far the following examples concern the abstract algebraic aspect of Tannaka duality only, which is narrated here as a consequence of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+Yoneda+lemma"} enriched Yoneda lemma
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
          %h3#ForPermutationRepresentations
            For
            = succeed "-Sets" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          %p
            A simple case of Tannaka duality is that of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            of a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (Tannaka duality for
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G Set
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-sets"} G-sets
              and
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi G
                    %mi Set
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    F \colon G Set \longrightarrow Set
            %p
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/forgetful+functor"} forgetful functor
              that sends a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/G-set"} G-set
              to its underlying
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/set"} set
            %p
              Then there is a canonical
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+homomorphism"} group-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Aut
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo ≃
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi G
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Aut(F) \;\simeq\; G
                    \\,.
            %p
              identifying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/automorphism+group"} automorphism group
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              (the group of invertible
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphisms"} natural isomorphisms
              from
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              to itself) with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .proof
            %h6#quick_proof Quick Proof
            %p
              Write
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo ≔
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mi G
                      %mo =
                      %mi G
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C \coloneqq Set^G = G Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi C
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F \colon C \to Set
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} representable
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo =
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F = C(G, -)
              by the regular
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msup
                      %mi Set
                      %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi G
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi G
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    End(F)
                    \=
                    Set^G(F, F)
                    \\cong
                    Set^G(C(G, -), C(G, -))
                    \\cong
                    C(G, G)
                    \\cong
                    G.
            %p
              The “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              ”‘s may denote the group
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              or its regular module. In particular, every endomorphism of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              is invertible. Hence,
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi End
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi Aut
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi F
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ≅
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(F) = Aut(F) \cong G
          .proof
            %h6#longwinded_proof Long-winded Proof
            %p We repeat the same proof, but with more notational details on what the entities involved in each step are precisely.
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              be the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi Set
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo =
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi op
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    G Set \;=\; Func(\mathbf{B}G^{op}, Set)
                    \\,.
            %p
              The canonical inclusion
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo :
                    %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i : {*} \to \mathbf{B}G
              induces the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi G
                    %mi Set
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Func(i,Set) : G Set \to Set
            %p
              which evaluates a functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %msup
                      %mi G
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho : \mathbf{B}G^{op} \to Set
              on the unique object of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              this is the same as homming out of the functor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/representable+functor"} represented by
              that unique object
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mi PSh
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Func(i,Set) = Hom_{PSh(\mathbf{B}G)}(Y_{\mathbf{B}G} {*}, -)
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo →
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y_{\mathbf{B}G} : \mathbf{B}G \to PSh(\mathbf{B}G)
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+embedding"} Yoneda embedding
            %p
              But this way we see that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Func(i,Set) : PSh(\mathbf{B}G) \to Set
              is itself a representable functor in the presheaf category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi PSh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi G
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} PSh(PSh(\mathbf{B}G)^{op})
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mrow
                          %mi PSh
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                            %mi B
                          %mi G
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi G
                    %mo *
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Func(i,Set) = Y_{\mathbf{PSh(\mathbf{B}G)^{op}}} Y_{\mathbf{B}G} *
                    \\,.
            %p
              So applying the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yoneda+lemma"} Yoneda lemma
              twice, we find that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi Aut
                              %mrow
                                %mi PSh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi PSh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi op
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi Func
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo ,
                            %mi Set
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                            %msub
                              %mi Aut
                              %mrow
                                %mi PSh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi PSh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi op
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mrow
                                  %mi PSh
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                    %mi B
                                  %mi G
                                  %msup
                                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                    %mi op
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Aut
                              %mrow
                                %mi PSh
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                                %msup
                                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                                  %mi op
                            %msub
                              %mi Y
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %msub
                              %mi Aut
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi G
                            %mo *
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≃
                            %mi G
                            %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                            %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    Aut_{PSh(PSh(\mathbf{B}G)^{op})} Func(i,Set)
                    \&amp; =
                    Aut_{PSh(PSh(\mathbf{B}G)^{op})} Y_{\mathbf{PSh(\mathbf{B}G)^{op}}} Y_{\mathbf{B}G} *
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Aut_{PSh(\mathbf{B}G)^{op}} Y_{\mathbf{B}G} *
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq
                    Aut_{\mathbf{B}G} *
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \simeq G
                    \\,.
                    \\end{aligned}
          %p
            Notice that the proof in no way used the fact that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            was assumed to be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
          %p
            But moreover, as the long-winded proof above makes manifest, even more abstractly the proof really only depended on the fact that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mi B
                  %mi G
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}G
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+category"} small category
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Tannaka duality for permutation representations of categories)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"} locally small category
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Rep
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi Func
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Rep_{Set}(C) := Func(C,Set)
              the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
              let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %msub
                      %mi Rep
                      %mi Set
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Set
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_c : Rep_{Set}(C) \to Set
              be the fiber-functor that evaluates at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi c
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
            %p
              Then we have a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Hom(F_c,F_{c'}) \simeq Hom_C(c,c')
                    \\,.
          %h3#ForVModules
            For
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+small+category"}> locally small
            )
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/closed+monoidal+category"} closed
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is enriched in itself via its
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+hom"} internal hom
          %p
            Observe that the setup, statement and proof of Tannaka duality for permutation representations given above is the special case for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V =
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
            of a statement verbatim the same in
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category+theory"} enriched category theory
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/functor+category"} functor category
            replaced everywhere by the
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
          %p
            Then the
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            as the monoid of endomorphisms of the forgetful
            = succeed "-functor" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                  %mi Mod
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
            to
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_3 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (Tannaka duality for
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "-algebras)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoid"} monoid
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/delooping"} delooping
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi B
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A Mod := [\mathbf{B}A,V]
            %p
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
              that encodes the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} End(F) := [F,F]
              of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor"} enriched functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi Rep
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : Rep(A) \to V
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} naturally isomorphic
              to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi F
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi A
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    End(A Mod \stackrel{F}{\to} V) \simeq A
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              We can repeat the argument given above for permutation representations, this time employing the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+Yoneda+lemma"} enriched Yoneda lemma
            %p
              First, recall that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B}A
              has a unique object. Identify the forgetful functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
              as the unique
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Fun
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %munder
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi Fun
                            %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                              %mi pt
                            %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi V
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⏟
                      %mrow
                        %mo ≅
                        %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\bullet]^*\colon\mathbf{Fun}_V(\mathbf{B}A,V)\to\underbrace{\mathbf{Fun}_V(\mathbf{pt}_V,V)}_{\cong V}
            %p
              given by precomposition along the
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi pt
                      %mi V
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\bullet]\colon\mathbf{pt}_V\to\mathbf{B}A
              \. Namely, it sends an
              = succeed "-module" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mi B
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M\colon\mathbf{B}A\to V
              to its evaluation
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi M
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo •
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M(\bullet) \in V
            %p Then by the enriched Yoneda lemma,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Nat
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %msub
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mi Nat
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mo •
                    %mo ,
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\mathbf{Nat}_V(Hom_{\mathbf{B}A}(-,\bullet),M)
                    \\cong
                    \\mathbf{Nat}_V(h_\bullet,M)
                    \\cong
                    M(\bullet)
            %p
              hence the functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [\bullet]^*
              is
              = succeed "-naturally" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "-functor" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Nat
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Nat}_V(h_\bullet,-)
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi End
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo =
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} def
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Nat
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi F
                            %mo ,
                            %mi F
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≅
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Nat
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo •
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo *
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %mo •
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                              %mo *
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≅
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Nat
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Nat
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi h
                              %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Nat
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi h
                              %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ≅
                              %mi Y
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Nat
                              %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi h
                              %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi h
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ≅
                              %mi Y
                            %msub
                              %mi h
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo =
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} def
                            %msub
                              %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                %mi Hom
                              %mrow
                                %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                                  %mi B
                                %mi A
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo •
                            %mo ,
                            %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo =
                              %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} def
                            %mi A
                            %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    End(F)
                    \&amp;\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}
                    \\mathbf{Nat}_V(F,F)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\cong
                    \\mathbf{Nat}_V([\bullet]^*,[\bullet]^*)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\cong
                    \\mathbf{Nat}_V(\mathbf{Nat}_V(h_{\bullet},-),\mathbf{Nat}_V(h_{\bullet},-))
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\overset{Y}{\cong}
                    \\mathbf{Nat}_V(h_{\bullet},h_{\bullet})
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\overset{Y}{\cong}
                    h_{\bullet}(\bullet)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}
                    \\mathbf{Hom}_{\mathbf{B}A}(\bullet,\bullet)
                    \\\
                    \&amp;\overset{\mathrm{def}}{=}
                    A,
                    \\end{aligned}
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              denotes the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+Yoneda+lemma"} enriched Yoneda lemma
              = succeed "-enriched" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat_{\mathbf{B}A \to V}
              whose objects are functors and morphisms are natural transformations; the embedding image of the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi h
                      %mo •
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi Cat
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi A
                        %mo →
                        %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h_{\bullet} \in Cat_{\mathbf{B}A \to V}
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi Nat
                        %mi V
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi h
                        %mo •
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{Nat}_V(h_{\bullet},-)
            %p
              Notice that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/endomorphism"} endomorphism
              object here is taken in the sense of enriched category theory, as described at
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (Categorical
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
                reconstruction of
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %p
              The monoid
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              can also be reconstructed as a categorical
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
              = succeed ";" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/end"} end
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi C
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi G
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    [C,D](F,G) = \int_{c \in C} D(F(c), G(c))
                    \\,.
            %p To spell it out in our case,
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi End
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi A
                        %mi Mod
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A \cong End(F) = \int_{N \in A Mod} V(F(N), F(N))
                    \\,.
          %p As before, the same proof shows the more general statement:
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_4 Theorem
            %p
              %strong
                (Tannaka duality for
                = succeed "-modules" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "-algebroids)" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              be a
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
              (a “
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              \-
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebroid"}> algebroid
              ”). Write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi C
                    %mo ,
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C Mod := [C,V]
              for the
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+functor+category"} enriched functor category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/object"} object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi C
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c \in C
              write
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi c
                    %mo :
                    %mi C
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_c : C Mod \to V
              for the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
              that evaluates at
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+isomorphism"} natural isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi hom
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi F
                      %mrow
                        %mi c
                        %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    hom(F_c, F_{c'}) \simeq C(c,c')
                    \\,.
          %p
            From this statement of Tannaka duality in
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %h4#ForPermuatationRepresentations For permutation representations
          %p
            The case of permutation representations is re-obtained by setting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V =
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
          %h4#ForAlgebraModules For algebra modules
          %p
            The general case of Tannaka duality for
            = succeed "-modules" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a{:href => "#ForVModules"} above
            restricts to the classical case of Tannaka duality for linear representations by setting
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V :=
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Vect"} Vect
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
          %p In this case the above says
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              %strong (Tannaka duality for linear modules)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebra"} algebra
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A Mod
              its category of
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mi Mod
                    %mo →
                    %mi Vect
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F : A Mod \to Vect
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber+functor"} fiber functor
